# =====================================================================
# myNotes Google Drive Cloud Storage Configuration
# =====================================================================
#
# OPTION 1 (RECOMMENDED FOR PUBLIC RELEASES / ZERO-SECRET DISTRIBUTIONS):
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deploy the included `worker/` directory to Cloudflare Workers (free tier).
# The Cloudflare Worker securely holds GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID and GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET
# in Cloudflare encrypted secrets, so NO client secret is ever baked into the
# distributed desktop app binary or visible to users who decompile the app.
#
# When AUTH_SERVER_URL is set, end users just click "Sign in with Google"
# and get instant 1-click cloud sync without entering any keys!
#
# Example:
# AUTH_SERVER_URL=https://mynotes-auth.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev
AUTH_SERVER_URL=

# OPTION 2 (DIRECT GOOGLE OAUTH FOR LOCAL DEVELOPMENT / DESKTOP PKCE):
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# If you don't want to run a Cloudflare Worker, you can connect directly
# using a Google Cloud OAuth 2.0 Client ID ("Desktop app" type).
#
# Steps to obtain credentials in Google Cloud Console:
# 1. Open https://console.cloud.google.com/
# 2. Create a project (or select an existing one)
# 3. Go to "APIs & Services" -> "Library" -> Enable "Google Drive API"
# 4. Go to "APIs & Services" -> "Credentials" -> "Create Credentials" -> "OAuth client ID"
#    - Application type: "Desktop app"
#    - Name: "myNotes Desktop"
# 5. Set your Client ID (and optional secret for direct code exchange):
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
